  "id": "childhood-disintegrative-disorder",
  "term": "childhood disintegrative disorder",
  "definition": "Childhood disintegrative disorder is a childhood condition in which development is normal for at least the first two years, followed by marked loss of previously gained abilities such as language, social interaction, bowel or bladder control, or motor skills. Repetitive, stereotyped behaviors similar to those seen in autism may also occur.",
